LIKEOS-EXPLORER(1)               User Commands              LIKEOS-EXPLORER(1)

NAME
       likeos-explorer - browse and manage files and folders

SYNOPSIS
       likeos-explorer [location...]
       likeos-explorer --version

DESCRIPTION
       likeos-explorer  is File Explorer, the desktop's file manager: the win-
       dow a folder opens in from the desktop, the Programs menu,  the  window
       manager's  menu  and  any  program that opens a folder (xdg-open).  The
       desktop itself stays PCManFM's.

       Each invocation opens a window, with a tab for every location given, or
       Home when none is.  A location is a folder (a path, a URI or ~/...),  a
       file  (its  folder  opens  with  the  file selected), trash:/// for the
       Trash, computer:/// for This PC, or likeos:home for Home.  A second in-
       vocation hands its locations to the running program  over  the  session
       bus, so all windows share one list of file operations, one undo history
       and one clipboard.

THE WINDOW
       Tabs   Each tab is a place of its own with its own history.

       Navigation bar
              Back, Forward (right-click for the history), Up and Refresh; the
              address  bar,  whose  crumbs  open their folder and whose arrows
              list the folders inside, and which turns into a text field on  a
              click  beside the crumbs; and the search box, which searches the
              folder shown and everything below it.

       Command bar
              New, Cut, Copy, Paste, Rename, Share, Delete,  Sort,  View,  and
              more  behind  the three dots.  What the selection does not allow
              is greyed out.  In the Trash it offers Empty Trash, Restore  and
              Restore all.

       Navigation pane
              Home,  the  personal  folders, Pinned (the GTK bookmarks, shared
              with every file dialog), This PC with its drives, Network when a
              backend provides it, and the Trash.  Files dropped on a row  are
              copied or moved there.

       Content
              Home  shows the pinned folders, the frequently used folders, Fa-
              vorites, the recently used files and the other places.  This  PC
              shows  the  drives  with their free space.  A folder is shown as
              Details, List, Compact, Icons, Large icons (with thumbnails)  or
              Tiles; the choice is remembered per folder.

       Details and preview panes
              The selected item's picture, type, size, dates and place, or its
              contents: an image, the beginning of a text, a video's frame and
              length.

   Searching
       Words  in  the search box must all appear in a name; case does not mat-
       ter.  * and ?  match any characters.  kind:image (or video, audio, doc-
       ument, folder, archive, program) and ext:png filter by kind and  exten-
       sion.   Below  the  home folder an index answers at once; elsewhere the
       folders are searched as the results come in.

KEYS
       Ctrl+T, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+N        new tab, close tab, new window
       Alt+Left, Alt+Right, Alt+Up   back, forward, up
       Ctrl+L, Alt+D, F4             edit the address
       Ctrl+F, Ctrl+E, F3            search
       F5                            refresh
       Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V        cut, copy, paste
       Ctrl+Shift+C                  copy the path
       F2                            rename
       Delete                        move to the Trash
       Shift+Delete                  delete permanently
       Ctrl+Shift+N                  new folder
       Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y                undo, redo
       Ctrl+A                        select all
       Alt+Enter                     properties
       Alt+P, Alt+Shift+P            preview pane, details pane
       Ctrl+H                        show hidden items
       Ctrl+Shift+2...8              the views of the View menu
       Ctrl+wheel                    smaller or larger view

       Typing a name in a folder selects the first item that starts with it.

FILE OPERATIONS
       Copies, moves, deletions and the rest run in the  background,  at  most
       two at a time and never two into the same folder at once.  An operation
       that  takes  more than a moment opens the File operations window, which
       shows each one's progress, speed and time left and can cancel it.

       When a name is taken at the destination, Explorer asks whether  to  re-
       place  the existing item, skip, keep both (the new item gets a number),
       or for two folders merge them, with a choice to answer the same way for
       the rest.  A failure can be retried, skipped  or  the  whole  operation
       cancelled.

       A  file  is copied under a hidden temporary name and renamed into place
       when complete, so an interrupted or cancelled copy leaves no half-writ-
       ten file.  A move between drives removes the original only when all  of
       it arrived.

       Undo  reverses the last copy, move, rename, new item, move to the Trash
       or restore: copies and new items go to the  Trash,  moved  and  renamed
       items  go  back,  trashed items are restored.  Deleting permanently and
       emptying the Trash cannot be undone.

FILES
       ~/.local/share/Trash
              The Trash (freedesktop.org layout).

       ~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
              Pinned folders.

       ~/.local/share/recently-used.xbel
              Recently used files, shared by every  program.   Folder  options
              can turn their display off or clear the list.

       ~/.cache/thumbnails
              Thumbnails, shared with the desktop.

       ~/.cache/likeos-explorer/index-v1
              The  search  index of the home folder.  Turned off in Folder op-
              tions, it is deleted.

       ~/.config/glib-2.0/settings/keyfile
              Settings (schema org.likeos.Explorer).

SEE ALSO
